.SS shutdown
.EX
void shutdown();
.EE
.PP
Stops every http.listen of the program, as SIGINT does
.SS listen
.EX
i32 listen(i32 port, Mux *mux, void *app = null, Options *opts = null);
.EE
.PP
Serves mux on port until SIGINT or SIGTERM (or http.shutdown()), then lets the requests in progress finish and returns 0; -1 with os.errno() set when the port can't be listened on. app reaches every handler as r.app. Runs a coroutine loop per CPU: handlers run on several threads at once, so what they share through app needs the atomic module or a lock. The mux is freed when listen returns.
